From: Graft64 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Common: include cstdlib for integer conversions

StringConv.h uses std::strtoll and std::strtoull. Include their defining
standard header rather than relying on transitive libc++ includes.

Authored locally against the locked FEX-2607 source after native ARM64 CI
failed with LLVM-MinGW 20260826. No code or patch was copied from another
project. This changes declarations only, not conversion semantics.

Upstream-Status: Pending (not submitted)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Common/StringConv.h b/FEXCore/Source/Common/StringConv.h
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Common/StringConv.h
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Common/StringConv.h
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <FEXCore/fextl/string.h>
 
 #include <concepts>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <string_view>
 
 namespace FEXCore::StrConv {
